  "journal": {
    "entry_id": "5ddcbb8fb0c69ffd36ae5bc3a0f2f3cb153419fe739fa3f09bc2cc29070be166",
    "text": "This session I read through the minbpe code to get oriented: lineage_bench.py, lineage_equiv.py, and the package files minbpe/base.py, basic.py, regex.py, gpt4.py and __init__.py, each in full. I made no edits and ran no sandbox evaluations.\n\nNothing was measured. The session stopped without submitting a change, so there is no candidate and no result to report.\n\nWhat I believe now is limited to what reading gives me. The tokenizers share helpers in base.py, with basic.py and regex.py layering training and encoding on top, and gpt4.py wrapping the regex tokenizer. The bench and equivalence scripts define what counts as a valid change. I have no numbers on where time goes, so any idea about hot spots is a guess.\n\nNext time I should start by running lineage_bench.py on unmodified code to get a baseline, then profile training and encoding to find the real cost. After that, make one focused edit, check it with lineage_equiv.py, and evaluate in the sandbox before submitting.",
